}]` matched nothing and did not test permissive provider-ID behavior.\n- The remaining 44 mutants are auditable kills with restored source.\n- Row 44 is constrained by exact returned and durable `SUCCEEDED` assertions after a delayed `PENDING` response.\n- Row 46 is constrained by the delayed call rejecting and the durable attempt retaining `re_current_provider`.\n- Row 47 is constrained by the exact truthful completion copy, live-region semantics, and focus assertion.\n- Row 48 is distinct from row 44: it proves a losing delayed caller rereads and returns the already-durable terminal status instead of throwing.\n- The final conditional transaction protects both attempt and aggregate refund state; existing assertions constrain ordinary persistence, terminal-state preservation, provider-ID conflicts, and transaction results.\n- No vacuous assertion or unmutated behavior gap was found.\n\nSkipped:\n\n- Production dependency audit: package and lock files are unchanged.\n- Container secret scan/probes: Dockerfile, standalone behavior, and sanitizer are unchanged.\n\nFinal integrity:\n\n- Exactly 12 intended modified and 4 intended untracked paths.\n- No staged or committed branch diff.\n- HEAD and `main` both `dab6bbf7cb63a49365daaa7e70508c458a5ab473`.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- `.next` absent.\n- Port 3000 free.\n- Both verifier scratch databases were removed; no verifier or mutant scratch database remains.\n- Existing `travel_app_refund_review_test` was preserved as requested.\n- Database and Mailpit containers are healthy.\n- Verification changed no tracked source.\n\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a007af-dc2d-7273-a829-7d59e29dc4f8"}}}
